\frac{\partial\mathcal L}{\partial\phi_z}
=
\frac{\partial\mathcal L}{\partial\phi},$ 其中 $\dot\phi=\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial t},
\qquad
\phi_x=\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x},
\qquad
\phi_y=\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial y},
\qquad
\phi_z=\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial z}.$ 如果$\mathcal L$包含多个场，则对每个场各应用一次该规则。结果就是运动方程组。

p.src:
Now add a scalar field $\phi$. The naive product $\Psi^\dagger\Psi\,\phi$ is not a Lorentz scalar. Inserting the same Dirac matrix that occurs in the mass term gives $\mathcal L_{\mathrm{int}}
\propto
\Psi^\dagger\beta\Psi\,\phi.$ Equivalently, $\Psi^\dagger\beta\Psi$ is the scalar Dirac bilinear. Varying the full Lagrangian adds a term proportional to $\phi$ to the Dirac equation and a source proportional to $\Psi^\dagger\beta\Psi$ to the scalar equation. The two fields scatter one another.

